   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "Cleveland was established on July 22, 1796, by surveyors of the Connecticut Land Company when they laid out Connecticut’s Western Reserve into townships and a capital city."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "The first permanent European settler in Cleveland was Lorenzo Carter, who arrived in May 1797 and built a cabin on the banks of the Cuyahoga River."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "Cleaveland oversaw the New England–style design of the plan for what would become the modern downtown area, centered on Public Square."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "Largely through the efforts of the settlement’s first lawyer, Alfred Kelley, the village of Cleveland was incorporated on December 23, 1814."
   },
   {
    "type": "sentence",
    "text": "The emerging community served as an important supply post for the U.S. during the Battle of Lake Erie in the War of 1812."
   },
